<p><em>I moved and trimmed your thread summary, since it was taking up extra space in the main forum screen. Try to keep thread descriptions (the text in the little box under the thread title) and titles short so you don't crowd out other authors in the forum listing. ~Zyn</em></p>
<p>**Update - 2-3-4 **</p>
<p><strong>Seeking green light:</strong> yes</p>
<p><strong>Page type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Page layout:</strong> Simple Camera log!</p>
<p><strong>Elevator pitch:</strong> This SCP is an sentient Small Pink teddy is generally kind and loving to any human that is around the age of 0 to 20 as long as it doesn't feel threatened or provoked.<br />
it has a ability to form a black space around it chest which shoots out an rope that seemingly telepathically controlled by this SCP. When provoked SCP use it ability to suffocate it opponent.<br />
It also can talk, walk and do varies activities with no problem.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Central&nbsp;Narrative</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Central&nbsp;narrative</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central narrative:</strong> The SCP was discovered when the Mother (Kathlyn White) of the owner (Mathilda White ) tried to throw it away after Mathilda's suicide. The mother was a researcher in the foundation and the SCP was quickly taken to the facility. The Plush had been with the owner since she was an infant and was unable to move until the day she took her life.</p>
<p>Kathlyn White (mother) worked as a researcher in the Foundation caused her to neglect her daughter. And may one of the reasons for her death. Mathilda's father died in a car accident when she was nine and her Uncle ended up looking after her most of the time since her mother too busy. But when Mathilda was sixteen her uncle died from lung disease. Including the fact she was bullied and didn't felt fit in. Incredibly lonely she spends her whole days just talking to her old Pink Plushie which she called it Pinkie, and over time her loneliness and depression got to her.</p>
<p>Every time looking and hearing Mathilda the SCP shows a sign of aging and is stitched up three or four times and its eyes are now gone ( and to time and brutal force of children tugging it). SCP is experiencing despair and uselessness but couldn't voice it and or even show it by movement, only the aging of the fabric of the SCP shows that both Mathilda and SCP mentality spiraling downhill.<br />
The years of resentment toward those who hurt Mathilda manifested into its consciousness and anomalous power.</p>
<hr />
<ul>
<li>Mathilda’s life prior to her death will shown by camera log! She’s doing it because her therapist suggested her to do it, we’ll see the interaction between her and SCP a lot.</li>
<li>In the camera log, we can see the SCP’s form degrading as Mathilda’s own mentality becoming unstable!</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention Grabber:</strong> The life line of the toys are our own life! When it cut, the toys will left shallow and will die away! It also about moving on after the loss of important other! Which the toy fails to do!</p>
